{"name":"Angel Falls","hex":"#a3bdd3","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Angel Falls","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A waterfall in the Canaima National Park, Venezuela; the highest waterfall in the world."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Angel_Falls"}],"entries":[{"title":"Angel Falls","blocks":[{"text":"Angel Falls  is a waterfall in Venezuela.\nIt is the world's tallest uninterrupted waterfall, with a height of 979 metres (3,212 ft), and a plunge of 807 m (2,648 ft). The waterfall drops over the edge of the Auyán-tepui mountain in the Canaima National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage Site in the Gran Sabana region of Bolívar State. The height figure, 979 m (3,212 ft), mostly consists of the main plunge but also includes about 400 metres (1,300 ft) of sloped cascade and rapids below the drop and then a 30-metre-high (100 ft) plunge downstream of these talus rapids."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e9/SaltoAngel1.jpg/330px-SaltoAngel1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angel_Falls","wikidata":"Q80299"},{"title":"Angel Falls (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"Angel Falls is an American drama television series created by Joyce Eliason, that aired on CBS from August 26 to September 30, 1993."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angel_Falls_(TV_series)","wikidata":"Q4762155"},{"title":"Angel","blocks":[{"text":"An angel is a spiritual, heavenly, or supernatural entity, often depicted as humanoid with bird-like wings, frequently in the role as a messenger or intermediary between God and humanity in various traditions like the Abrahamic religions. Other roles include protectors and guides for humans, such as guardian angels, and servants of God. In Western belief-systems the term is often used to distinguish benevolent from malevolent intermediary beings."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/02/Angel_of_the_Annunciation_MET_DP167921.jpg/330px-Angel_of_the_Annunciation_MET_DP167921.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Angel","wikidata":"Q235113"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Salto_Chur%C3%BAn_Mer%C3%BA.JPG/500px-Salto_Chur%C3%BAn_Mer%C3%BA.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Salto_Chur%C3%BAn_Mer%C3%BA.JPG/1280px-Salto_Chur%C3%BAn_Mer%C3%BA.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7e/Salto_Chur%C3%BAn_Mer%C3%BA.JPG/500px-Salto_Chur%C3%BAn_Mer%C3%BA.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aerial view of Dragon Falls (Churún Merú), a waterfall 10 km south of Angel Falls at 5°52′32″N 62°32′07″W﻿ / ﻿5.87556°N 62.53528°W﻿ / 5.87556; -62.53528","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASalto_Chur%C3%BAn_Mer%C3%BA.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Lacascadamasbelladelmunto.jpg/500px-Lacascadamasbelladelmunto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Lacascadamasbelladelmunto.jpg/500px-Lacascadamasbelladelmunto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALacascadamasbelladelmunto.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Angel_falls_panoramic_20080314.jpg/500px-Angel_falls_panoramic_20080314.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fc/Angel_falls_panoramic_20080314.jpg/500px-Angel_falls_panoramic_20080314.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_c